  "id": "nachi_no_dengaku",
  "name": "Nachi no Dengaku (Nachi shrine field-music ritual)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Nachi no Dengaku is a ritual performing art of the Kumano Nachi Taisha shrine in Nachikatsuura, presented each July at the Nachi fire festival; it descends from medieval dengaku, the field music of rice-planting rites, and is inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Dancers play binzasara, a clapper of strung wooden slats, and small drums, led by a flute. The auxiliary-percussion card stands in for the binzasara and the membrane-drum card for the drums.",
